proof.text:
Let $(d',h'_1,h'_2)$ be another such common dense refinement. Apply [det-nagata-refinement-common-dense] to $d,d'$ to get a dense $d''$ with maps $k:d''\to d$, $k':d''\to d'$. For each $a$, $h_ak$ and $h'_ak'$ are $Y$-morphisms $d''\to c_a$ restricting to the given $j_a$ on $X$. They are equal by clause (3) of [det-nagata-refinement-morphisms], whose hypothesis is scheme-theoretic density of the source $d''$, not mere topological density and not density of $c_a$. Step 4 now gives, as natural transformations,
$$\rho_{h_2}^{-1}\rho_{h_1}
=(\rho_k\rho_{h_2})^{-1}(\rho_k\rho_{h_1})
=\rho_{h_2k}^{-1}\rho_{h_1k}
=\rho_{h'_2k'}^{-1}\rho_{h'_1k'}
=(\rho_{k'}\rho_{h'_2})^{-1}(\rho_{k'}\rho_{h'_1})
=\rho_{h'_2}^{-1}\rho_{h'_1}.$$
Each equality after Step 4 is associativity and cancellation of an isomorphism with its inverse. Thus the comparison is independent of the common dense refinement, including its projection maps.
